align:Persona-Autonomous_AI_Agent a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Autonomous_AI_Agent"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Autonomous_AI_Agent" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Autonomous_AI_Agent.md> ;
    skos:definition "The Autonomous AI Agent is an orchestration framework that coordinates specialized analytics and knowledge services to support decision-making. This very fast moving expertise is currently being used to create configurable workflows that integrate evidence from many data domains in both preclinical and clinical. Execution is scheduled and event-driven (e.g., on data updates or defined intervals) and can include sequential and parallel AI agents to deliver an agreed end goal such as literature retrieval, data summaries or analysis of data. It's success at the intended task depends on how the AI is instructed, the suitability of the AI model used and the FAIR characteristics of the underlying data—being findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable—with semantic standards (ontologies, identifiers), well-defined schemas and mappings, and machine-actionable metadata." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Autonomous_AI_Agent.md> ;
    align:sourceText "The Autonomous AI Agent is an orchestration framework that coordinates specialized analytics and knowledge services to support decision-making. This very fast moving expertise is currently being used to create configurable workflows that integrate evidence from many data domains in both preclinical and clinical. Execution is scheduled and event-driven (e.g., on data updates or defined intervals) and can include sequential and parallel AI agents to deliver an agreed end goal such as literature retrieval, data summaries or analysis of data. It's success at the intended task depends on how the AI is instructed, the suitability of the AI model used and the FAIR characteristics of the underlying data—being findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable—with semantic standards (ontologies, identifiers), well-defined schemas and mappings, and machine-actionable metadata." .

align:Persona-Business_Analyst a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Business_Analyst"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Business_Analyst" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Business_Analyst.md> ;
    skos:definition "The Business Analyst (BA) bridges business stakeholders and delivery teams to elicit, analyze, and communicate requirements, define as‑is / to‑be processes, and ensure solutions meet intended business outcomes. The BA coordinates with Business/Domain [Data Stewards](Data_Steward.md) and [Data Standards and Governance Experts](Data_Standards_and_Governance_Expert.md), so that the scope and acceptance criteria align with agreed data definitions, quality expectations, and organisational policies. Core competencies include stakeholder analysis, requirements engineering, process analysis, testing coordination, facilitation, and communication." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Business_Analyst.md> ;
    align:sourceText "The Business Analyst (BA) bridges business stakeholders and delivery teams to elicit, analyze, and communicate requirements, define as‑is / to‑be processes, and ensure solutions meet intended business outcomes. The BA coordinates with Business/Domain [Data Stewards](Data_Steward.md) and [Data Standards and Governance Experts](Data_Standards_and_Governance_Expert.md), so that the scope and acceptance criteria align with agreed data definitions, quality expectations, and organisational policies. Core competencies include stakeholder analysis, requirements engineering, process analysis, testing coordination, facilitation, and communication." .

align:Persona-Business_Leader a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Business_Leader"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Business_Leader" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Business_Leader.md> ;
    skos:definition "In an organization, personnel holding roles such as CEO, CFO, CTO, COO, or Functional Line Leaders with executive and strategy level decision- making capacities." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Business_Leader.md> ;
    align:sourceText "In an organization, personnel holding roles such as CEO, CFO, CTO, COO, or Functional Line Leaders with executive and strategy level decision- making capacities." .

align:Persona-Business_Owner a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Business_Owner"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Business_Owner" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Business_Owner.md> ;
    skos:definition """The Business Owner is an executive-level business role accountable for the value, performance, and strategic success of a defined business process, product, system, or dataset. As the designated authority within their domain, the Business Owner ensures that data and processes deliver measurable business value, meet defined KPIs, and align with organizational objectives and regulatory requirements.

    In accordance with DAMA-DMBOK2, the Business Owner is responsible for defining business requirements, approving data standards and policies, and ensuring that data is managed as a strategic enterprise asset. They collaborate with Data Stewards, Architects, and IT teams to translate business needs into data capabilities, oversee the quality and fitness-for-purpose of data, and drive continuous improvement.

    By championing sound data governance and FAIR-aligned practices, the Business Owner ensures that information assets are consistent, compliant, and reusable—enabling efficient decision-making, regulatory confidence, and sustained business value generation across the organization.""" ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Business_Owner.md> ;
    align:sourceText """The Business Owner is an executive-level business role accountable for the value, performance, and strategic success of a defined business process, product, system, or dataset. As the designated authority within their domain, the Business Owner ensures that data and processes deliver measurable business value, meet defined KPIs, and align with organizational objectives and regulatory requirements.

    In accordance with DAMA-DMBOK2, the Business Owner is responsible for defining business requirements, approving data standards and policies, and ensuring that data is managed as a strategic enterprise asset. They collaborate with Data Stewards, Architects, and IT teams to translate business needs into data capabilities, oversee the quality and fitness-for-purpose of data, and drive continuous improvement.

    By championing sound data governance and FAIR-aligned practices, the Business Owner ensures that information assets are consistent, compliant, and reusable—enabling efficient decision-making, regulatory confidence, and sustained business value generation across the organization.""" .

align:Persona-Citizen_Data_Scientist a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Citizen_Data_Scientist"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Citizen_Data_Scientist" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Citizen_Data_Scientist.md> ;
    skos:definition "Non-expert business user applying self-service analytics tools and dashboards; highly competent but not data-science trained. Individual within an organization who, despite lacking formal training in data science, utilizes data analysis tools and techniques to extract insights from data. These individuals often come from various backgrounds, such as business, marketing, or operations, and possess domain-specific expertise. Citizen Data Scientists leverage self-service analytics platforms, intuitive data visualization tools, and automated machine learning algorithms and Autonomous AI agents to explore datasets, generate reports, and uncover patterns or trends relevant to their roles." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Citizen_Data_Scientist.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Non-expert business user applying self-service analytics tools and dashboards; highly competent but not data-science trained. Individual within an organization who, despite lacking formal training in data science, utilizes data analysis tools and techniques to extract insights from data. These individuals often come from various backgrounds, such as business, marketing, or operations, and possess domain-specific expertise. Citizen Data Scientists leverage self-service analytics platforms, intuitive data visualization tools, and automated machine learning algorithms and Autonomous AI agents to explore datasets, generate reports, and uncover patterns or trends relevant to their roles." .

align:Persona-Clinical_Data_Manager a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Clinical_Data_Manager"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Clinical_Data_Manager" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Clinical_Data_Manager.md> ;
    skos:definition "Ensures accuracy, integrity, and reliability of data collected during clinical trials. They are responsible for designing and maintaining data management plans, overseeing data collection systems, and implementing quality control processes to ensure compliance with regulatory standards and requirements (e.g. from FDA,EMA). They manage the end-to-end data lifecycle in clinical trials." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Clinical_Data_Manager.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Ensures accuracy, integrity, and reliability of data collected during clinical trials. They are responsible for designing and maintaining data management plans, overseeing data collection systems, and implementing quality control processes to ensure compliance with regulatory standards and requirements (e.g. from FDA,EMA). They manage the end-to-end data lifecycle in clinical trials." .

align:Persona-Curator a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Curator"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Curator" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Curator.md> ;
    skos:definition "Organizes, standardises, integrates, and maintains ontologies, vocabularies, datasets and data products to ensure they are FAIR and aligned with governance standards." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Curator.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Organizes, standardises, integrates, and maintains ontologies, vocabularies, datasets and data products to ensure they are FAIR and aligned with governance standards." .

align:Persona-Data_Analyst a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Analyst"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Analyst" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Analyst.md> ;
    skos:definition "Data Analyst is responsible for designing, developing, and maintaining dashboards and recurring reports that support business needs." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Analyst.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Data Analyst is responsible for designing, developing, and maintaining dashboards and recurring reports that support business needs." .

align:Persona-Data_Engineer a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Engineer"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Engineer" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Engineer.md> ;
    skos:definition "A Data Engineer builds and maintains the infrastructure needed for data collection, storage, and processing. They design data pipelines, optimize databases, manage large-scale data architectures, and ensure data quality and reliability throughout the analytics process." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Engineer.md> ;
    align:sourceText "A Data Engineer builds and maintains the infrastructure needed for data collection, storage, and processing. They design data pipelines, optimize databases, manage large-scale data architectures, and ensure data quality and reliability throughout the analytics process." .

align:Persona-Data_Integration_Specialist a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Integration_Specialist"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Integration_Specialist" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Integration_Specialist.md> ;
    skos:definition "A Data Integration Specialist focuses on combining data from different sources, ensuring that data from various systems can work together. Their main tasks include designing ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) processes, creating data mappings, and solving integration issues so data flows smoothly between platforms." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Integration_Specialist.md> ;
    align:sourceText "A Data Integration Specialist focuses on combining data from different sources, ensuring that data from various systems can work together. Their main tasks include designing ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) processes, creating data mappings, and solving integration issues so data flows smoothly between platforms." .

align:Persona-Data_Owner a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Owner"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Owner" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Owner.md> ;
    skos:definition "A Data Owner  has both the legal rights and managerial responsibility for a dataset. The Data Owner is responsible for establishing policies on who can access and use the data, ensuring compliance with relevant laws and standards, and managing permissions. They oversee the assignment of metadata, documentation, and maintenance of data quality, while ultimately being accountable for the dataset’s proper stewardship, even if routine management is delegated to others, ensuring the data remains FAIR-compliant at all times." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Owner.md> ;
    align:sourceText "A Data Owner  has both the legal rights and managerial responsibility for a dataset. The Data Owner is responsible for establishing policies on who can access and use the data, ensuring compliance with relevant laws and standards, and managing permissions. They oversee the assignment of metadata, documentation, and maintenance of data quality, while ultimately being accountable for the dataset’s proper stewardship, even if routine management is delegated to others, ensuring the data remains FAIR-compliant at all times." .

align:Persona-Data_Protection_Officer a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Protection_Officer"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Protection_Officer" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Protection_Officer.md> ;
    skos:definition "The Data_Protection_Officer (DPO) ensures compliance with privacy, regulatory, and security requirements, acting as the operational lead for data protection practices. While this role may overlap with the [Legal_Data_Expert](Legal_Data_Expert.md), the DPO is distinct in its focus on implementation and enforcement, rather than legal advisory or framework creation. A [Legal_Data_Expert](Legal_Data_Expert.md) typically has a background in law and focuses on developing legal guidelines, while the DPO specializes in applying these guidelines to operational activities." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Protection_Officer.md> ;
    align:sourceText "The Data_Protection_Officer (DPO) ensures compliance with privacy, regulatory, and security requirements, acting as the operational lead for data protection practices. While this role may overlap with the [Legal_Data_Expert](Legal_Data_Expert.md), the DPO is distinct in its focus on implementation and enforcement, rather than legal advisory or framework creation. A [Legal_Data_Expert](Legal_Data_Expert.md) typically has a background in law and focuses on developing legal guidelines, while the DPO specializes in applying these guidelines to operational activities." .

align:Persona-Data_Quality_Manager a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Quality_Manager"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Quality_Manager" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Quality_Manager.md> ;
    skos:definition "Defines, monitors, and remediates data quality issues; maintains quality, freshness, observability and completeness of enterprise data." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Quality_Manager.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Defines, monitors, and remediates data quality issues; maintains quality, freshness, observability and completeness of enterprise data." .

align:Persona-Data_Scientist a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Scientist"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Scientist" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Scientist.md> ;
    skos:definition "Data Scientists  find, compile, clean, preprocess and analyze complex datasets. They interpret data trends, develop predictive models, and communicate findings to inform strategic decision-making. Data Scientists also design experiments, possess expertise in statistical methods, programming, data visualization, database management, and may have domain-specific knowledge. See also “researcher” ." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Scientist.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Data Scientists  find, compile, clean, preprocess and analyze complex datasets. They interpret data trends, develop predictive models, and communicate findings to inform strategic decision-making. Data Scientists also design experiments, possess expertise in statistical methods, programming, data visualization, database management, and may have domain-specific knowledge. See also “researcher” ." .

align:Persona-Data_Standards_and_Governance_Expert a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Standards_and_Governance_Expert"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Standards_and_Governance_Expert" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Standards_and_Governance_Expert.md> ;
    skos:definition """Acts as a governance advisor and facilitator, ensuring the adoption and compliance of data standards across the organization.
    Provides expertise on data standards and governance within a specific business function.
    Defines how data is managed, protected, and used across the enterprise by establishing policies, standards, and roles that ensure data is accurate, secure, compliant with regulations, and aligned with business objectives.""" ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Standards_and_Governance_Expert.md> ;
    align:sourceText """Acts as a governance advisor and facilitator, ensuring the adoption and compliance of data standards across the organization.
    Provides expertise on data standards and governance within a specific business function.
    Defines how data is managed, protected, and used across the enterprise by establishing policies, standards, and roles that ensure data is accurate, secure, compliant with regulations, and aligned with business objectives.""" .

align:Persona-Data_Steward a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Steward"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Steward" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Steward.md> ;
    skos:definition """Data stewardship encompasses the set of practices that ensure data is properly collected, stored, maintained, and shared throughout its entire lifecycle. FAIR data stewardship extends traditional data management by introducing a coordinated framework that ensures data is (or becomes) and remains compliant to Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable (FAIR) principles.
    The core responsibilities of a Data Steward vary widely, ranging from policy development and advisory functions to operational, technical, and IT-related activities. These responsibilities may differ across research-performing and data-driven organizations, where job titles and scopes of work may also vary. Data stewardship roles can be coordination-focused, policy-oriented, research-oriented, or infrastructure-oriented, depending on organizational needs and maturity. A Data Steward may also serve as a lead role within a data governance initiative, taking ownership of data assets and collaborating with business and technical stakeholders to define and implement governance objectives. This role is closely linked to maintaining data integrity and control within data governance and master data management frameworks.""" ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Steward.md> ;
    align:sourceText """Data stewardship encompasses the set of practices that ensure data is properly collected, stored, maintained, and shared throughout its entire lifecycle. FAIR data stewardship extends traditional data management by introducing a coordinated framework that ensures data is (or becomes) and remains compliant to Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable (FAIR) principles.
    The core responsibilities of a Data Steward vary widely, ranging from policy development and advisory functions to operational, technical, and IT-related activities. These responsibilities may differ across research-performing and data-driven organizations, where job titles and scopes of work may also vary. Data stewardship roles can be coordination-focused, policy-oriented, research-oriented, or infrastructure-oriented, depending on organizational needs and maturity. A Data Steward may also serve as a lead role within a data governance initiative, taking ownership of data assets and collaborating with business and technical stakeholders to define and implement governance objectives. This role is closely linked to maintaining data integrity and control within data governance and master data management frameworks.""" .

align:Persona-Data_Strategy_Owner a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Data_Strategy_Owner"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Data_Strategy_Owner" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Strategy_Owner.md> ;
    skos:definition "A senior leader responsible for defining, developing, and executing an organization's overarching data strategy to align with business goals. This role translates business strategy into a data strategy, establishing the roadmap for how data will be collected, managed, governed, and leveraged to drive value and innovation across the company." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Data_Strategy_Owner.md> ;
    align:sourceText "A senior leader responsible for defining, developing, and executing an organization's overarching data strategy to align with business goals. This role translates business strategy into a data strategy, establishing the roadmap for how data will be collected, managed, governed, and leveraged to drive value and innovation across the company." .

align:Persona-FAIR_Community_Manager a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR_Community_Manager"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "FAIR_Community_Manager" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/FAIR_Community_Manager.md> ;
    skos:definition """An individual or group responsible for facilitating and managing a community of practice (CoP). The organizer’s role involves coordinating meetings, events, and activities for the community, creating channels for communication and knowledge sharing, and fostering a supportive and inclusive environment where members feel comfortable exchanging ideas and experiences. They may also be involved in recruiting new members, setting goals and objectives for the community, and ensuring that it remains vibrant and relevant to its members’ needs and interests.

    Person who organizes groups of people around shared aims - see https://the-turing-way.netlify.app/collaboration/research-infrastructure-roles/community-manager.html\"""" ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/FAIR_Community_Manager.md> ;
    align:sourceText """An individual or group responsible for facilitating and managing a community of practice (CoP). The organizer’s role involves coordinating meetings, events, and activities for the community, creating channels for communication and knowledge sharing, and fostering a supportive and inclusive environment where members feel comfortable exchanging ideas and experiences. They may also be involved in recruiting new members, setting goals and objectives for the community, and ensuring that it remains vibrant and relevant to its members’ needs and interests.

    Person who organizes groups of people around shared aims - see https://the-turing-way.netlify.app/collaboration/research-infrastructure-roles/community-manager.html\"""" .

align:Persona-FAIR_Data_Architect a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR_Data_Architect"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "FAIR_Data_Architect" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/FAIR_Data_Architect.md> ;
    skos:definition "A role in an organization focusing on processes, models and policies that manages the generation, use and governance of data, metadata  and data standards in a FAIR compliant manner. Develops processes to deliver and maintain FAIR data and services" ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/FAIR_Data_Architect.md> ;
    align:sourceText "A role in an organization focusing on processes, models and policies that manages the generation, use and governance of data, metadata  and data standards in a FAIR compliant manner. Develops processes to deliver and maintain FAIR data and services" .

align:Persona-FAIR_Trainer a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "FAIR_Trainer"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "FAIR_Trainer" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/FAIR_Trainer.md> ;
    skos:definition "Trainers design and deliver training programs to a variety of stakeholders ranging from researchers to business leaders and project teams across organisation functions (R&ED, but also development, clinical, franchises), with a focus on awareness and best practice implementation of FAIR data principles. The role supports compliance with corporate data governance policies, regulatory expectations, and scientific needs. It interfaces and interacts with data governance leads, technology leaders, data architects, community managers, and researcher teams to align training content with organizational FAIR maturity and priorities." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/FAIR_Trainer.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Trainers design and deliver training programs to a variety of stakeholders ranging from researchers to business leaders and project teams across organisation functions (R&ED, but also development, clinical, franchises), with a focus on awareness and best practice implementation of FAIR data principles. The role supports compliance with corporate data governance policies, regulatory expectations, and scientific needs. It interfaces and interacts with data governance leads, technology leaders, data architects, community managers, and researcher teams to align training content with organizational FAIR maturity and priorities." .

align:Persona-Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen.md> ;
    skos:definition "This role emerges  in organizations with high FAIR maturity (levels 4–5) and broad, well-curated data ecosystems, where interoperable, reusable data products are fully embedded into daily operations. Highly educated domain expert empowered by FAIR data products (e.g. query services, knowledge graphs) to find information in complex (FAIR) data sets daily decisions. Organization member who is empowered with access to information, possesses critical thinking skills, enabling them to contribute effectively to the organization’s goals and objectives." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Knowledge-Enabled_Citizen.md> ;
    align:sourceText "This role emerges  in organizations with high FAIR maturity (levels 4–5) and broad, well-curated data ecosystems, where interoperable, reusable data products are fully embedded into daily operations. Highly educated domain expert empowered by FAIR data products (e.g. query services, knowledge graphs) to find information in complex (FAIR) data sets daily decisions. Organization member who is empowered with access to information, possesses critical thinking skills, enabling them to contribute effectively to the organization’s goals and objectives." .

align:Persona-Lab_Manager a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Lab_Manager"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Lab_Manager" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Lab_Manager.md> ;
    skos:definition "Oversees the daily operation of research or testing laboratories, ensuring that experiments, equipment, personnel, and data workflows run efficiently, safely, and in compliance with regulatory and quality standards. They coordinate between scientists, data teams, and quality or regulatory functions to maintain accurate experimental records, ensure data integrity, and optimize resource utilization. The role combines scientific leadership with operational and digital oversight, increasingly relying on data-driven decision-making to improve productivity and reproducibility. The role may include a wide range of responsibilities, including budget and spends, overseeing daily operations, ensuring safety, managing lab and IT equipments and supplies, and supervising staff." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Lab_Manager.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Oversees the daily operation of research or testing laboratories, ensuring that experiments, equipment, personnel, and data workflows run efficiently, safely, and in compliance with regulatory and quality standards. They coordinate between scientists, data teams, and quality or regulatory functions to maintain accurate experimental records, ensure data integrity, and optimize resource utilization. The role combines scientific leadership with operational and digital oversight, increasingly relying on data-driven decision-making to improve productivity and reproducibility. The role may include a wide range of responsibilities, including budget and spends, overseeing daily operations, ensuring safety, managing lab and IT equipments and supplies, and supervising staff." .

align:Persona-Legal_Data_Expert a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Legal_Data_Expert"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Legal_Data_Expert" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Legal_Data_Expert.md> ;
    skos:definition "Provides legal and regulatory expertise to ensure data is managed, shared, and reused in compliance with privacy, consent, and intellectual property requirements, while supporting FAIR-aligned practices across the organization.Has expertise in privacy law, data governance, and intellectual property; ability to draft and interpret data sharing agreements; experience in regulatory compliance and ethical data use in research and business contexts." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Legal_Data_Expert.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Provides legal and regulatory expertise to ensure data is managed, shared, and reused in compliance with privacy, consent, and intellectual property requirements, while supporting FAIR-aligned practices across the organization.Has expertise in privacy law, data governance, and intellectual property; ability to draft and interpret data sharing agreements; experience in regulatory compliance and ethical data use in research and business contexts." .

align:Persona-Master_Data_Manager a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Master_Data_Manager"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Master_Data_Manager" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Master_Data_Manager.md> ;
    skos:definition """Role ensuring authoritative single sources of truth across the enterprise (e.g., products, customers, materials). Manages the master data in a given business domain. Responsible for managing vocabularies, code lists, and ontologies to ensure consistency and semantic alignment. Manages reference data to ensure master data from multiple sources are aligned.
    An Enterprise Data Steward manages and enforces data governance policies at an enterprise level, bridging the gap between business users, data owners, and IT. They ensure that enterprise-wide data assets are properly defined, cataloged, and maintained.""" ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Master_Data_Manager.md> ;
    align:sourceText """Role ensuring authoritative single sources of truth across the enterprise (e.g., products, customers, materials). Manages the master data in a given business domain. Responsible for managing vocabularies, code lists, and ontologies to ensure consistency and semantic alignment. Manages reference data to ensure master data from multiple sources are aligned.
    An Enterprise Data Steward manages and enforces data governance policies at an enterprise level, bridging the gap between business users, data owners, and IT. They ensure that enterprise-wide data assets are properly defined, cataloged, and maintained.""" .

align:Persona-Ontologist a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Ontologist"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Ontologist" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Ontologist.md> ;
    skos:definition "An expert in knowledge representation and ontology building," ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Ontologist.md> ;
    align:sourceText "An expert in knowledge representation and ontology building," .

align:Persona-Project_Manager a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Project_Manager"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Project_Manager" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Project_Manager.md> ;
    skos:definition "Coordinates -cross-functional- efforts to deliver projects or initiative on time, within budget, and in compliance with regulatory standards. They oversee projects in -or spanning- research, clinical development, manufacturing, regulatory submissions, and commercialization domains. Acting as the connective link between scientific, operational, and business teams, the Project Manager ensures alignment of objectives, resources, and timelines , including across the drug development lifecycle. They manage risk, track milestones, and facilitate decision-making through clear reporting and proactive issue resolution. In addition, they drive collaboration among internal teams, external partners, and vendors while ensuring adherence to GxP and quality standards." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Project_Manager.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Coordinates -cross-functional- efforts to deliver projects or initiative on time, within budget, and in compliance with regulatory standards. They oversee projects in -or spanning- research, clinical development, manufacturing, regulatory submissions, and commercialization domains. Acting as the connective link between scientific, operational, and business teams, the Project Manager ensures alignment of objectives, resources, and timelines , including across the drug development lifecycle. They manage risk, track milestones, and facilitate decision-making through clear reporting and proactive issue resolution. In addition, they drive collaboration among internal teams, external partners, and vendors while ensuring adherence to GxP and quality standards." .

align:Persona-Reference_Data_Manager a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Reference_Data_Manager"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Reference_Data_Manager" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Reference_Data_Manager.md> ;
    skos:definition "A Reference Data Manager is responsible for overseeing the management, quality, and governance of reference data within an organization. This role ensures that reference data (such as codes, classifications, and standard lists) is accurate, consistent, and aligned with business needs. The Reference Data Manager defines data standards, maintains master/reference data sets, monitors data quality, and implements processes that ensure data is FAIR. They collaborate with business units, data stewards, and technology teams to support data governance, resolve data issues, and enable reliable analytics and reporting." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Reference_Data_Manager.md> ;
    align:sourceText "A Reference Data Manager is responsible for overseeing the management, quality, and governance of reference data within an organization. This role ensures that reference data (such as codes, classifications, and standard lists) is accurate, consistent, and aligned with business needs. The Reference Data Manager defines data standards, maintains master/reference data sets, monitors data quality, and implements processes that ensure data is FAIR. They collaborate with business units, data stewards, and technology teams to support data governance, resolve data issues, and enable reliable analytics and reporting." .

align:Persona-Researcher a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Researcher"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Researcher" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Researcher.md> ;
    skos:definition "A person engaged in conducting research, possibly recognized as an occupation by a formal job title. While a researchers produces and uses data, they are not necessarily data scientists (see: data scientist)." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Researcher.md> ;
    align:sourceText "A person engaged in conducting research, possibly recognized as an occupation by a formal job title. While a researchers produces and uses data, they are not necessarily data scientists (see: data scientist)." .

align:Persona-Subject_Matter_Expert a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Subject_Matter_Expert"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Subject_Matter_Expert" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Subject_Matter_Expert.md> ;
    skos:definition "Deep domain expert who consumes and validates FAIR data rather than managing it. A subject matter expert (SME) is a person with deep domain knowledge, often as a practitioner of the area of knowledge. SME are often consulted by knowledge engineers and ontologists in what is known as ‘knowledge elicitation exercice’ to express use cases and concepts which are then organized and modeled in semantic artifact by knowledge engineers. (NB: SME also stands for Small to Medium Enterprise)." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Subject_Matter_Expert.md> ;
    align:sourceText "Deep domain expert who consumes and validates FAIR data rather than managing it. A subject matter expert (SME) is a person with deep domain knowledge, often as a practitioner of the area of knowledge. SME are often consulted by knowledge engineers and ontologists in what is known as ‘knowledge elicitation exercice’ to express use cases and concepts which are then organized and modeled in semantic artifact by knowledge engineers. (NB: SME also stands for Small to Medium Enterprise)." .

align:Persona-Technology_Leader a owl:NamedIndividual,
        align:Persona ;
    rdfs:label "Technology_Leader"@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "Technology_Leader" ;
    dcterms:source <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Technology_Leader.md> ;
    skos:definition "CIO/CTO/CDO-level role shaping enterprise technology and digital strategy. The most senior executive in an enterprise who works with information technology and computer systems, in order to support enterprise goals.  May also drive digital transformations in a company or an organization. For example by  converting traditional \"analog\" businesses to ones relying on digital workflows and infrastructure. The CDO is responsible for whole process of digital transformation." ;
    align:inFrameworkVersion align:FAIRMM-v1.2.5 ;
    align:primarySource <https://github.com/Pistoia-Alliance-Inc/FAIR-Maturity-Matrix/blob/8ff4676eb340b0da5034ffb3d0e901c594c3cfc4/docs/FAIR_personas/Technology_Leader.md> ;
    align:sourceText "CIO/CTO/CDO-level role shaping enterprise technology and digital strategy. The most senior executive in an enterprise who works with information technology and computer systems, in order to support enterprise goals.  May also drive digital transformations in a company or an organization. For example by  converting traditional \"analog\" businesses to ones relying on digital workflows and infrastructure. The CDO is responsible for whole process of digital transformation." .

